      </imageobject>
    </mediaobject>
  </informalfigure>
  <important>
    <title>Host name for registration</title>
    <para>
      The host name is used for the registration with the &scc;. If you do not set a host name,
      your system will be registered with the transient host name <literal>agama</literal>.
      Even if the system is assigned a new host name later, it will not automatically get
      updated in the &scc;. Therefore setting host name is recommended.
    </para>
    <para>
      To update the host name in the &scc; after the registration, first change the system's
      host name, then deregister it with &suseconnect; and register it again under the new
      host name.
    </para>
  </important>
  <tip>
    <title>Identifying systems in the &scc;</title>
    <para>
      If you have multiple systems registered with the same host name in the &scc;, it is difficult
      to tell them apart. To identify a system, use it's UUID instead. You can find it under
      <guilabel>Hardware information</guilabel> in the &scc; and on the system by running
      <command>dmidecode -s system-uuid</command>.
    </para>
  </tip>
